From 1f6c3d86c8f73e2a892092722dbc12faedd243d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:43:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-17: hide a component in the designer only -- the
 eye of the WPF document outline (0.17.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pages stack many panels at one place (Alert.Note: a dozen pop-up panels at
160,290), so the ones underneath could not be seen or clicked.
- The component tree has an eye on every row: hide in the designer / show
  again (eye-closed); the title bar has "show all" while something is hidden.
  The design surface's right-click menu has the same toggle for the selection.
- The probe hides it with a rule of its own ([data-htd-hide] { visibility:
  hidden !important }): a click at its place reaches what is underneath, the
  tree's own "(hidden)" (no layout box) is not affected, the DFM comparison
  (display) neither.
- Never written to the source: kept per page in the workspace state, so it
  survives Reload and reopening; the form itself cannot be hidden.
- The tree marks it "（設計時隱藏）" with a dimmed eye-closed icon.

Tests: lib 103, probe (hidden = invisible and a click goes through, shown
again, no edit), smoke 66 (probe told the whole set, tree mark, kept per page,
form refused, show all, no WorkspaceEdit), panels, real VS Code 69 (hidden in
the real designer, still hidden after Reload, show all, page never dirty).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
